      "id": "syn_interpretive_questions_ef9055b41ae4",
      "kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "facts": [
        "The best-known reading is 666, while Papyrus 115 and other witnesses support an ancient 616 variant.",
        "The two beasts enact coercive rule, worship, deception, and economic exclusion in a Danielic and Roman symbolic field.",
        "Roman imperial power, civic religion, and economy are major historical contexts, but Revelation does not name a single emperor as the complete key.",
        "Nero Caesar calculated in Hebrew letters is a leading explanation of 666 and can accommodate 616 by spelling, but alternatives remain.",
        "The book calls its hearers to endurance and witness, not to enact its divine judgment scenes through religious violence."
